<title>BELGIUM: Ter Beke says swine fever ups pork prices.</title>
<headline>Ter Beke says swine fever ups pork prices.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Luc De Bruyckere, chief executive officer of Belgian meat products maker Ter Beke NV, said on Tuesday the outbreak of swine fever in pig farms in the Netherlands and Germany was unjustifiably pushing up pork prices in Belgium.</p>
<p>&quot;It is starting to affect our supplies in terms of price,&quot; De Bruckere told Reuters in a telephone interview. &quot;The Belgian market is not yet touched by the fever but people are very concerned...and on an emotional basis prices have gone up.&quot;</p>
</text>
